---
import BaseLayout from '@versal/ui/BaseLayout';
---

<BaseLayout site="main" title="Privacy Policy" canonical="https://jsonversal.com/privacy/">
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="text-muted">Effective date: 2026-09-10 · Last updated: 2026-09-10</p>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All tools run 100% on your device. We do not collect, log, or transmit the data you process.</li>
    <li>We run no analytics and set no cookies.</li>
    <li>The site makes no third-party requests at runtime — no CDN, no analytics beacon, no tracking pixels.</li>
    <li>The only thing we store is your light/dark theme preference, held locally on your device.</li>
    <li>We do not sell or share your personal information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Information collected</h2>
  <p>None of the data you submit to our tools leaves your browser. We have no server-side processing for tool inputs. There are no accounts, no sign-up and no user profiles.</p>

  <h2>Analytics and cookies</h2>
  <p>We run no analytics of any kind, and this site sets no cookies. There is no visitor counting, no fingerprinting and no cross-site tracking — not even in aggregate form. Because nothing is collected, there is nothing to consent to and nothing to opt out of.</p>

  <h2>Local storage</h2>
  <p>We store a single item in your browser's local storage: your light/dark theme preference. It stays on your device, is never transmitted to us, and can be cleared at any time from your browser settings. This falls under the "strictly necessary" exemption of ePrivacy Article 5(3), which is why no consent banner is shown.</p>

  <h2>Third-party requests</h2>
  <p>
    Loading an asset from a third-party CDN discloses your IP address to that provider. We avoid this
    entirely:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Fonts</strong> — Geist and Geist Mono are self-hosted from this domain. We do not use Google Fonts or any other font CDN.</li>
    <li><strong>JavaScript libraries</strong> — bundled or self-hosted; none are fetched from a public CDN at runtime.</li>
    <li><strong>Everything else</strong> — there is none. No analytics beacon, no advertising, no social widgets, no embedded third-party media.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>See <a href="/licenses/">Licenses &amp; Third-Party Notices</a> for the full attribution list.</p>

  <h2>Where data is processed</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare is a US-headquartered provider, so serving a page
    involves processing connection metadata (including your IP address) on infrastructure that may be
    located outside your country. For transfers out of the EEA/UK we rely on Cloudflare's data processing
    addendum incorporating the European Commission's Standard Contractual Clauses, together with the
    technical measures described above. We do not sell personal data and do not use it for advertising.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    If you are in the European Economic Area, the UK or Switzerland, you have the right to access, rectify
    or erase your personal data, to restrict or object to processing, and to data portability. If you are a
    California resident, you have the right to know what personal information is collected and to opt out of
    its sale or sharing — we do neither. Because we hold no personal data about you at all, most requests
    resolve to confirming we hold nothing. You may contact us at any time to exercise
    these rights, and you may lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>This site is a developer tool aimed at a professional audience and is not directed at children under 16.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy we will update the "Last updated" date above. Material changes will be noted on the homepage.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or requests: <a href="mailto:hello@jsonversal.com">hello@jsonversal.com</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
